%% Source: .github/workflows/ci.yml, .github/workflows/deploy.yml, vercel.json,
%% prisma/seed.ts (main), prisma/seedGuard.ts, scripts/smoke.mjs, docs/OPERATIONS.md ("Seeding production once"),
%% tests/helpers/db.ts (the test database is seeded by the tests).
%% The seed is NOT a step of either workflow: it is run by hand once per new environment.
%% GitHub settings (branch protection, the reviewer on the "production" environment) are not repository files: not verified here.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Dev as Developer
    participant GH as GitHub
    participant CI as CI workflow (ci.yml)
    participant DP as Deploy workflow (deploy.yml)
    actor Rev as Reviewer (production environment)
    participant V as Vercel CLI
    participant DB as Production PostgreSQL (PROD_DIRECT_URL)
    participant APP as Deployed app
    participant SM as Smoke test (curl /api/health/ready)

    Dev->>GH: push to main (or pull request)
    GH->>CI: lint, typecheck, build, test (Postgres 16 service), audit (npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high)
    CI->>CI: test job: create pfc_app, prisma migrate deploy on it, npm test on pfc_test
    CI-->>GH: all jobs succeed
    GH->>DP: workflow_run completed, conclusion success, event push, branch main
    DP->>Rev: job uses environment production, waits for approval
    Rev-->>DP: approves
    DP->>DP: checkout the exact head_sha CI passed on, npm ci, install vercel CLI
    DP->>V: vercel pull --environment=production
    DP->>V: vercel build --prod
    DP->>DB: npx prisma migrate deploy (before the new code goes live)
    Note over DP,DB: Previous release still serves traffic on the new schema, so migrations must be backward compatible
    DP->>V: vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod
    V-->>DP: deployment URL
    DP->>SM: GET URL/api/health/ready, retry 6 times, 10 s apart
    SM->>APP: request (x-vercel-protection-bypass only if the secret is set)
    APP->>DB: SELECT 1 (healthRepository.pingDatabase)
    APP-->>SM: 200 status ok, or 503 status unavailable
    SM-->>DP: pass or fail the job

    Note over Dev,DB: Seeding a new environment, by hand, once (docs/OPERATIONS.md)
    Dev->>Dev: set DATABASE_URL = DIRECT_URL, SEED_CONFIRM_HOST, SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD, SEED_DEMO_PASSWORD in the shell only
    Dev->>Dev: npx prisma db seed (prisma/seed.ts)
    Note over Dev,DB: checkSeedTarget runs first, before anything connects to the database
    alt DIRECT_URL and DATABASE_URL name different hosts, or neither is a valid URL
        Dev-->>Dev: Refusing to seed
    else host is localhost, in SEED_ALLOWED_HOSTS, or equals SEED_CONFIRM_HOST
        Note over Dev,DB: checkSeedPasswords
        alt host only allowed through SEED_CONFIRM_HOST (private target)
            alt either password variable missing, shorter than 12, equal to the other, or a published demo password
                Dev-->>Dev: Refusing to seed (names the variable and rule, never a value)
            else both valid
                Dev->>DB: upsert demo accounts and data with the two private passwords
                Dev-->>Dev: prints Seeding host only
            end
        else localhost or SEED_ALLOWED_HOSTS
            Dev->>DB: upsert demo data (published passwords unless the variables are set and valid)
        end
    else any other host
        Dev-->>Dev: Refusing to seed, naming the host and the way out
    end
    Dev->>SM: npm run smoke -- production URL --expect-seed
